  "uncertainties": [
    "The 2026-09-15 v1.12.0 Normal run cleared in 10:14 from battlefield entry, with about 9:42 of active combat, zero deaths, 104 completed weapon skills, no add-wave weapon skill sent to Bigwig, and all five Phantom Whorls absorbed by shadows. Both three-add waves killed the Astrologer in 53-56 seconds and the final Tormentor in 115-121 seconds. One transient three-target convergence on Kickpuncher cleared after the runtime stopped his lane, but this remains a Difficult promotion risk. Version 1.13.0 changes only the pre-pull boundary so arming prepares in place until an exact manual Bigwig pull is observed; it awaits one Normal validation.",
    "The Cait profile is also not claimed proven for this exact party; the two isolated variants must be evaluated independently.",
    "There is no documented or observed proximity damage modifier. Bigwig is now allowed to follow its Dolo/Kick holder into the focus; formation quality and frontal-cone exposure still require live observation.",
    "A successful Blue Magic or Flash result proves a tag on that exact add, not continuing hate ownership; the runtime records that distinction but does not gate combat on it.",
    "Bars and the current runtime infer a monster's current target from the primary target of its latest direct melee or TP action rather than a hidden enmity table. Hostile spell targets and pickup action results are deliberately excluded from ownership proof. The seven-second Bigwig signal is strong but not omniscient; a five-second review balances transfer latency against assignment thrash.",
    "A Bigwig hate change can transiently overlap the old parked assignment before the next review and pickup succeeds. PartyOps must measure hostile target convergence around every holder transfer.",
    "All Qutrub in this battlefield are documented as Weight immune, so no Indi-Gravity, Weight status, or movement-slow evidence belongs in the strategy.",
    "All encounter enemies are documented Sleep immune; Sheep Song remains an enmity action, never crowd control.",
    "A completed Astrologer Sleep-family cast is the earliest reliable wake trigger available; Curaga II is scheduled best effort and does not prove every target was in range.",
    "Fresh Colure Active buff 612 following an exact Indi-Wilt result confirms the aura transaction on Tackle but does not prove potency; neither action nor status can gate combat.",
    "Enemy-targeting Indicolure requires both Achoo and Tackle to be on each add's enmity list; add-side eligibility and practical Wilt coverage remain live-test questions.",
    "The profile deliberately avoids a GEO Diaga lane because cross-hate is unnecessary and conflicts with the explicit two-target budget.",
    "Tackle's current shield, damage-taken set, and route have not been demonstrated against a five-add VD physical pack.",
    "The capacity allocation is complete for Normal's three-add set. Difficult and Very Difficult have additional off-focus adds and remain unproven; the profile does not impose a software difficulty gate.",
    "The current plan assumes the kill focus counts as one potential hostile target for every attacker even when its live target is someone else; actual current-target timelines must be checked rather than inferred from attack participation alone.",
    "Violent Flourish is a bounded reactive attempt rather than a guaranteed Triple Reversal stun; the adapter prevents requests without finishing stock or a ready recast, but resistance, interruption, range failure, and unresolved outcomes remain possible.",
    "The four non-mage characters currently have no recognized Reraise item in Inventory; their automatic Reraise lane becomes effective only after an eligible item is supplied and never blocks arming.",
    "PartyOps observed Triple Reversal as action ID 3982 in the salvaged clear, but installed Windower resources still do not provide stable names for every Qutrub monster ability; live policy continues resolving the action through the packet resource name when available.",
    "Cure analysis must distinguish nominal healing, effective recovery, and overheal without feeding telemetry back into live policy.",
    "Any future tuning belongs in a new isolated no-Cait profile version and must not modify the Cait Sith runtime or adapter."
  ]
}
